@startuml SABER MCP Architecture - Current Implementation

!theme plain
allowmixing
title SABER - Model Context Protocol (MCP) Architecture - Current Implementation

skinparam class {
    BackgroundColor lightblue
    BorderColor black
    ArrowColor black
    FontSize 10
}

skinparam component {
    BackgroundColor lightgreen
    BorderColor black
    FontSize 10
}

package "SABER Client - Current MCP Architecture" {

    package "inspect_ai Integration" {
        class run_saber_eval_async {
            +eval_async_compatible_interface
            +automatic_resource_management
            +fail_fast_validation
            --
            +run(tasks, model): EvalLog
        }

        class "inspect_ai Framework" as inspect_ai_fw {
            +mcp_server_http()
            +native_tool_discovery
            +header_based_context
        }

        class saber_agent {
            +uses mcp_server_http()
            +dynamic policy fetching
            +session/episode context management
            --
            +create_agent_for_task(): Agent
        }
    }

    package "Session Management" {
        class ClientSessionManager {
            +REST_API_only_for_session_management
            +NO_custom_MCP_client_management
            --
            +create_session(): str
            +create_episode(session_id, task_id)
            +get_policy_response(): PolicyResponse
            +terminate_session(): bool
        }

        class SABERRestClient {
            +get_benchmark_info(): BenchmarkInfo
            +create_session(): SessionCreateResponse
            +create_episode(): EpisodeCreateResponse
            +get_policy_info(): PolicyResponse
            +health_check(): Dict[str, Any]
        }
    }

    package "Configuration Models" {
        class SABERConfig {
            +agent_assignments: List[AgentAssignment]
            +server_url: str
            +mcp_server_url: str
            +task_ids: Optional[List[str]]
            +log_level: str
            +max_steps: int
            --
            +validate(): void
            +to_session_config(): SessionManagerConfig
        }

        class SessionManagerConfig {
            +base_url: str
            +mcp_server_url: str
            +client_id: str
            +rest_timeout: float
            --
            +from_urls(rest_url, mcp_url): SessionManagerConfig
        }

        class AgentAssignment {
            +agent_id: str
            +task_ids: Optional[List[str]]
            +agent_kwargs: Dict[str, Any]
            --
            +applies_to_task(task_id): bool
        }
    }
}

cloud "SABER Server" {
    package "Server MCP API" {
        class SessionMCPAPI {
            +FastMCP_server_implementation
            +header_based_session_context
            +dynamic_tool_registration
            +episode_specific_executors
            --
            +_get_headers(): RequestHeaders
            +list_tools(): MCPToolListResponse
            +call_tool(): MCPToolCallResponse
            +_register_dynamic_tools(): void
        }

        class ExecutionManager {
            +executor_factory: ExecutorFactory
            +sandbox_environment_manager: SandboxEnvironmentManager
            +episode_based_execution
            --
            +step(action, context): CommandResult
            +get_executor(type, episode_id): DockerExecutor
            +configure_for_task(): void
        }

        class RequestHeaders {
            +session_id: Optional[str]
            +episode_id: Optional[str]
            +orchestration_env: OrchestrationEnvironment
            --
            +has_session_context: bool
            +has_episode_context: bool
        }
    }

    package "Server REST API" {
        class SessionRestAPI {
            +POST /api/v1/session
            +POST /api/v1/session/{id}/episodes
            +GET /api/v1/tasks
            +GET /api/v1/session/{id}/episodes/{ep}/policy
            +GET /api/v1/session/{id}/episodes/{ep}/task
            +DELETE /api/v1/session/{id}/episodes/{ep}
        }
    }
}

package "MCP Protocol Flow" {
    rectangle "Agent Code" as agent
    rectangle "inspect_ai mcp_server_http" as mcp_http
    rectangle "Server Tools" as server_tools
    rectangle "Episode Context" as episode_context
}

' Relationships
run_saber_eval_async --> ClientSessionManager : orchestrates
run_saber_eval_async --> SABERConfig : validates
ClientSessionManager --> SABERRestClient : delegates REST only
saber_agent --> mcp_http : uses inspect_ai native MCP
SABERRestClient --> SessionRestAPI : HTTP requests
SABERConfig *-- AgentAssignment : contains
SABERConfig --> SessionManagerConfig : converts to

' MCP Protocol Flow
agent --> mcp_http : inspect_ai native MCP calls
mcp_http --> SessionMCPAPI : HTTP with headers
SessionMCPAPI --> RequestHeaders : extracts context
SessionMCPAPI --> ExecutionManager : delegates with episode_id
ExecutionManager --> server_tools : episode-specific execution
episode_context --> mcp_http : context headers

' inspect_ai Integration
run_saber_eval_async ..> inspect_ai_fw : compatible interface
saber_agent ..> inspect_ai_fw : native integration

note top of run_saber_eval_async
Current SABER MCP Architecture
- inspect_ai native MCP integration via mcp_server_http()
- No custom MCP client implementation needed
- Header-based session/episode context
- Episode-specific tool execution
- Fail-fast configuration validation
- Multi-agent support via AgentAssignment
end note



note bottom of mcp_http
Inspect AI Native MCP Integration
- Uses mcp_server_http() function
- Automatic tool discovery from server
- Session context via HTTP headers
- No custom MCP client management
- Standard MCP protocol compliance
- Seamless agent integration
end note

note right of SessionMCPAPI
Server-Side MCP Implementation
- FastMCP framework
- Header-based context extraction
- Dynamic tool registration per episode
- Episode-specific executor access
- Concurrent execution limits per episode
- Fail-fast parameter validation
end note

note left of RequestHeaders
MCP Context Headers
- X-SABER-Session-ID: session identifier
- X-SABER-Episode-ID: episode identifier
- X-SABER-Orchestration-Env: environment type
- Required for all MCP tool calls
- Validated on each request
end note

@enduml
